abstract: >-
  This repository contains the source code, templates, configuration,
  publication metadata, documentation and structured literary content
  supporting Verse & Variable, an independent Indian literary journal.
  The publication is devoted to poetry, shayari, ghazals, nazms,
  literary prose, philosophical expressions and other forms of Indian
  literary expression across India's diverse languages and traditions.
  Its initial linguistic foundation comprises Urdu, Hindi, Marathi,
  Kannada, Tamil, Malayalam and Telugu. The editorial approach
  emphasises literary integrity, accurate attribution, cultural and
  linguistic context, thoughtful interpretation and original English
  commentary. The journal's publication scope is literary. Scientific
  knowledge and specialist expertise may inform individual explorations
  when genuinely relevant, but are not compulsory editorial elements
  or independent publication categories. The repository supports the
  journal's multilingual digital archive and its long-term presentation
  through Jekyll and GitHub Pages.

